// jhonstart/plugin — the render-plugin point (front 30, decisions 113 and 114).
//
// jhonstart declares the point, awaits it at the three moments CSS has to be
// written and once more for the plugin's payload contribution, and is its
// only caller; the CSS bridge member of this workspace implements it over
// its stylesheet's `flush()`. The core names no plugin, no stylesheet library
// and no key a plugin may give.
//
// A plugin is a RECORD OF FUNCTIONS, not the `behavior` the README sketches:
// an `Array<RenderPlugin>` of two different implementing types does not type
// (`type mismatch: expected Rec, got Quiet`, measured 2026-09-26 against
// compiler `248d0896`), and `app(plugins: [...])` needs exactly that array.
// The four methods are the four fields, each asynchronous, and `name` is what
// a failure names.
//
// The order is the caller's, so it is jhonstart's (`render.bp` implements it):
//
//   1. `head()` ONCE, after the shell (or the whole page) rendered, before the
//      head is serialised; its string goes into `<head>`.
//   2. `chunk(holeId)` per streamed boundary, after it rendered and before its
//      markup is written; its string goes FIRST inside the fill's
//      `<template data-jh-f="…">`, with no marker of its own.
//   3. `close()` at the end, after the last chunk; an `Error` fails the render.
//   4. `payload()` ONCE, after `close`; `[]` contributes nothing, one pair
//      writes its JSON text under its key. A render key (every key of
//      `contracts.md § 2` but `s`) or a key two plugins give fails the render.
//
// Each call is awaited before the next moment begins, and plugins are called
// in the order `app` received them.

// JSON text a plugin serialised, written verbatim.
pub type Json = string;

pub type RenderPlugin(
    name: string,
    head: fn() -> @Task<string>,
    chunk: fn(holeId: string) -> @Task<string>,
    close: fn() -> @Task<@Result<void, string>>,
    payload: fn() -> @Task<Array<#(string, Json)>>,
)
